      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:6:14",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ وَقْتُ الْمَغْرِبِ فِي السَّفَرِ إِلَى رُبُعِ اللَّيْلِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Salma Bin Al Khattab, from Muhammad Bin Al Waleed, from Aban Bin Usman, from Umar Bin Yazeed, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The time for Al-Maghrib during the journey is up to a quarter of the night’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "14. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Salmah ibn al-Khattab from Muhammad ibn al-Walid from Aban ibn ‘Uthman from ‘Umar ibn Yazid who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The time for al-Maghrib Salah (prayer) on a journey remains until passing of one-fourth of the night.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
